{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Different Shades Of Blue feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels because guitar-driven blues is what I want to hear right now.",
    "I Still Do connects with my interest in Eric Clapton, while Imagine fits the familiar classic-rock side of my listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Wallflower and 25 do not fit this visit because softer vocal music and contemporary pop do not offer the blues-guitar sound I am seeking.",
    "50th Anniversary Collection and Definitive Collection give me too little information about the music to feel confident choosing either, and I am not seeking a greatest-hits collection today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in established artists seems to have been stretched into an interest in collections, although familiar names alone do not make those albums appealing today.",
    "My interaction with Blown Away makes country suggestions understandable, but it does not mean I want country collaborations during this visit."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection between Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels matters especially because I currently want guitar-driven blues, rather than anything broadly related to familiar artists.",
    "I rarely choose something unless it feels particularly relevant. Different Shades Of Blue gives me enough reason to try one album; even another plausible Clapton album can wait."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in familiar rock and blues, but spread too broadly beyond the guitar-driven blues I want right now."
}"}
